# Changelog

## [v0.5] - Categorized Inventory, Options & Full Keyboard/Mouse Navigation

### Added
* **Categorized Item & Inventory System (`Item`, `GameContext`)**
  * Created `Item` record (`id`, `name`, `description`, `category`) and implemented `GameContext.inventory` as a `LinkedHashMap<String, List<Item>>` with `addItem(Item)` and `getItems(String)` helpers (including an `"All"` aggregate view and starter items).
* **Tabbed Split-Pane Menus (`SplitListScene`)**
  * Added `SplitListScene` extending `Scene` to render a dual-pane layout (items/options list on the left, live description preview on the right) with dynamic top category tabs shared by **Inventory** and **Options**.
  * Generated inventory tabs dynamically from `GameContext.inventory.keySet()` and added an **Options** menu with a `"General"` tab containing a **Return to Title Screen** action.
* **Overlay Navigation & History (`SceneManager`)**
  * Added `previousScene` tracking, `openOverlay(String)`, `returnToPrevious()`, and boolean feedback from `handleChoice(int)` so toggling Inventory or Options returns directly to the prior gameplay scene.
* **Persistent Utility Bar & Full Input Support (`Renderer`)**
  * Added persistent **Inventory [I]** and **Options [Esc]** buttons below the 4-choice action bar (disabled on the Title Screen, and collapsing the choice bar automatically while inside overlays).
  * Added full keyboard controls: `1`–`4` (and Numpad `1`–`4`) for direct choice selection, `Arrow` keys to navigate choices or scroll list entries, `Tab` / `Shift + Tab` to cycle category tabs, `Enter` / `Space` to confirm selections, `I` to toggle Inventory, and `Esc` to toggle Options.
  * Added standard mouse interaction in list menus: single-click to highlight and preview descriptions, and primary double-click to execute selected items or options.

### Changed
* Removed the disabled `"Open inventory"` placeholder choice from `village_square` in `scenes.json` in favor of the dedicated bottom bar button and `I` shortcut.
* Bumped `GameContext.version` to `v0.5`.

## [v0.4] - Data-Driven JSON Scene Loading

### Added
* **JSON Scene Pipeline (`scenes.json`, `SceneData`)**
  * Added Gson dependency (`com.google.code.gson:gson:2.11.0`) to `app/build.gradle`.
  * Created `SceneData` and `ChoiceData` records to deserialize external scene definitions from `src/main/resources/scenes.json`.
  * Added `SceneManager.loadScenesFromJson(String)` to parse JSON rooms, map string action keys (`INCREMENT_LOOK`) and `targetScene` IDs into `Choice` callbacks, and dynamically interpolate `{lookCounter}` placeholders in scene text.

### Changed
* Migrated `village_square` and `villager_chat` definitions out of hardcoded Java registrations in `SceneManager` and into `src/main/resources/scenes.json`.
* Bumped `GameContext.version` to `v0.4`.

## [v0.3] - Abstract Scene Base Class & Centralized Registration

### Changed
* **Abstract `Scene` Architecture**
  * Converted `Scene` from an interface into an `abstract class` that stores `textProvider` and `choicesProvider` directly, providing overloaded constructors for static values and `GameContext`-driven lambdas while preserving `getText` and `getChoices`.
  * Simplified `ExplorationScene` and `TitleScene` to extend `Scene` and delegate text and choice management to `super(...)`, removing duplicate provider fields.
  * Updated `TitleScene` banner text to dynamically read `GameContext.version`.
* **Centralized Scene Registration (`SceneManager`)**
  * Moved `registerScenes()` from `Game` into `SceneManager` (called automatically upon initialization), allowing choice callbacks to invoke `switchTo(...)` directly without extra manager references.
  * Simplified `Game.start()` to initialize core components and switch directly to `"title"`.
  * Bumped `GameContext.version` to `v0.3`.

## [v0.2] - Scene Caching & Data-Driven Exploration

### Added
* **Scene Caching & ID Routing (`SceneManager`)**
  * Added `HashMap<String, Scene>` scene cache with `getOrCreate(String, Supplier<Scene>)`, `registerScene(String, Scene)`, `clearCache()`, and ID-based `switchTo(String)` navigation.
  * Wired up `Scene.onEnter(GameContext)` lifecycle hook during scene transitions.
* **Reusable `ExplorationScene` Class**
  * Created a generic, data-driven `ExplorationScene` supporting both static text/choices and context-aware providers (`Function<GameContext, ...>`), preparing the engine for external JSON scene loading.
* **New Dialogue Scene (`"villager_chat"`)**
  * Enabled the **Talk to villager** choice in the village square, leading to an interactive villager encounter with navigation back to `"village_square"`.

### Changed
* Replaced the hardcoded `TestExplorationScene` with two pre-registered `ExplorationScene` instances (`"village_square"` and `"villager_chat"`) initialized on startup in `Game`.
* Updated `TitleScene` and exploration choices to transition strictly by string scene ID rather than instantiating new `Scene` objects on every switch.
* Bumped `GameContext.version` to `v0.2`.


## [v0.1] - Initial Release

### Added

* **Core Engine & State Management**
* Implemented `Scene` interface with lifecycle hooks (`onEnter`, `onExit`) and state-driven text/choice rendering.
* Implemented `SceneManager` to coordinate active scenes, player choices, and UI refreshes.
* Added `GameContext` to maintain shared game state across scenes (including `lookCounter` and version metadata).
* Created `Choice` action wrapper supporting `Consumer<GameContext>` callbacks and enabled/disabled states.

* **JavaFX User Interface**
* Built `Renderer` featuring a read-only, word-wrapped `TextArea` for narrative output and a dynamic 4-button `HBox` choice bar.
* Configured `Game` JavaFX application entry point and `App` launcher class.

* **Playable Scenes**
* **Title Scene (`TitleScene`):** Added main menu with working **New Game** and **Quit** options, plus placeholder slots for **Continue** and **Options**.
* **Test Exploration Scene (`TestExplorationScene`):** Added a village square scene with a working **Look around** interaction counter, **Return to title** navigation, and placeholder buttons for **Talk to villager** and **Open inventory**.

### Fixed

* Corrected an off-by-one bounds check (`index >= 0`) in `SceneManager.handleChoice` so the first choice button (`index 0`) triggers properly.
